  "instance_name": "cultural_relativism",
  "label": "Cultural Relativism",
  "description": "The meme implicitly challenges the viewer to consider whether cultural practices should be judged by external standards. It suggests that if alcohol is banned in one culture (Islamic), it should also be banned in another (Western), implying a moral equivalence. This requires understanding of the concept of cultural relativism — the idea that cultural norms should be understood within their own context rather than judged by external standards — which is often used to critique such comparisons.",
